<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-SEIZINGER WINS SUPER-G AT WORLD CUP FINALS.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SEIZINGER WINS SUPER-G AT WORLD CUP FINALS.</headline>
<dateline>VAIL, Colorado 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Katja Seizinger of Germany won the women's Super-G at the World Cup Finals on Thursday, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Hilde Gerg finished second to clinch the season's title and Martina Ertl claimed third to complete a German sweep.  </p>
<p>The results were declared official.</p>
</text>
